    description: "C# keyword types and Swift module-qualified types hash apart from their other spelling.\n\nREPRO: C# void f(string s) vs void f(System.String s); Swift func f(_ x: Swift.Int) vs func f(_ x: Int). Neither is decided by imports, so WI-palus left both as written; C# global:: prefix not checked either. Decide whether the language's built-in alias table should canonicalize them. Found by PR 5 agent 4 (stable-id v17 branch, 2026-11-20) while building WI-palus (type names hashed through the file's imports): ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/fast_smart_test_build_11172026/pr5/palus/RESULTS.md section 6; repros in pr5/palus/residual_probe/."  # badd
